https://publications.artic.edu/pissarro/reader/paintingsandpaper/section/8\">https://publications.artic.edu/pissarro/reader/paintingsandpaper/section/8</a>.\\n\\nFonsmark, Anne-Birgitte. Pissarro: et møde på Skt. Thomas, exh. cat. (Ordrupgaard Museum, 2017), 163, 193, fig. 156 (ill.). \\n\\nClarisse Fava-Piz and Nerina Santorius, The Honest Eye: Camille Pissarro\\'s Impressionism, exh. cat. (Munich; London; New York: Prestel, 2025), 15, 60, 64 (color ill.), 243, cat. 13.',\n",
       "   'exhibition_history': \"Paris, Palais des Champs-Élysées, Salon de 1866, May 1–June 20, 1866, cat. 1564, as Bords de la Marne en hiver.\\n \\nParis, Musée de l’Orangerie, Centenaire de la naissance de Camille Pissarro, Feb.–Mar. 1930, cat. 3.\\n\\nChicago, Renaissance Society of the University of Chicago, Fifth Annual Exhibition of Modern French Painting, Feb. 7–21, 1932, cat. 23.\\n\\nPossibly Glasgow Art Gallery, The Spirit of France: French Paintings of the Nineteenth and Twentieth Centuries, June 1943, cat. 38.\\n\\nLondon, Lefevre Gallery, French Masters, XIX and XX Century, June–July 1952, cat. 13 (ill.).\\n\\nNew York, Wildenstein, C. Pissarro, Mar. 25–May 1, 1965, cat. 2 (ill.).\\n\\nColumbus, Ohio, Dr. Howard Sirak, Feb. 18–Feb. 25, 1975, no cat.\\n\\nHighland Park, Ill., Neison Harris, Mar. 7–May 21, 1975, no cat.\\n\\nPhiladelphia Museum of Art, The Second Empire, 1852–1870: Art in France under Napoleon III, Oct. 1–Nov. 26, 1978, cat. VI-96 (ill.); Detroit Institute of Arts, Jan. 18–Mar. 18, 1979; Paris, Galeries Nationales d’Exposition du Grand Palais, as L’art en France sous le Second Empire, May 11–Aug. 13, 1979, cat. 264 (ill.).\\n\\nLondon, Hayward Gallery, Pissarro: Camille Pissarro 1830–1903, Oct. 30, 1980–Jan. 11, 1981, cat. 6 (ill.); Paris, Galeries Nationales du Grand Palais, Jan. 30–Apr. 27, 1981; Museum of Fine Arts, Boston, May 19–Aug. 9, 1981.\\n\\nLos Angeles County Museum of Art, A Day in the Country: Impressionism and the French Landscape, June 28–Sept. 16, 1984, cat. 9 (ill.); Art Institute of Chicago, Oct. 23, 1984–Jan. 6, 1985; Paris, Galeries Nationales d’Exposition du Grand Palais, as L’impressionnisme et le paysage français, Feb. 4–Apr. 22, 1985.\\n\\nParis, Galeries Nationales du Grand Palais, Impressionnisme: Les origines, 1859–1869, April 19–August 8, 1994, cat. 156; New York, Metropolitan Museum of Art, Origins of Impressionism, September 27, 1994–January 8, 1995.\\n\\nArt Gallery of New South Wales, Camille Pissarro,