       "   'publication_history': 'Art Institute of Chicago, The Arthur Jerome Eddy Collection of Modern Paintings and Sculpture, exh. cat. (Chicago: The Art Institute of Chicago, 1931), 22, cat. 13.\\n\\nArt Institute of Chicago, A Century of Progress Exhibition of Paintings and Sculpture, exh. cat. (Chicago: The Art Institute of Chicago, 1933), 82, cat. 761.\\n\\nPeter Selz, German Expressionist Painting (Berkeley: University of California Press, 1957), 209, pl. 89.\\n\\nArt Institute of Chicago, Paintings in the Art Institute of Chicago: A Catalogue of the Picture Collection (Chicago: Art Institute of Chicago, 1961), 342.\\n\\nThe German Expressionists and Their Contemporaries: 50 Years of Fantasy and Frenzy, exh. cat. (South Bend, IN.: University of Notre Dame, Art Gallery, 1969), n.p., cat. 84a.\\n\\nGerman and Austrian Expressionism: Art in a Turbulent Era, exh. cat. (Chicago: Museum of Contemporary Art, 1978), 29, no cat. no.\\n\\nExpressionism and Its Legacy: German Art from 1905 to the Present: The Frankfurter Kunstkabinett Hannah Bekker vom Rath, exh. cat. (St. Petersburg, FL.: Museum of Fine Arts, 1980), n.p., cat. 9.\\n\\nAnne Mochon, Gabriele Münter, between Munich and Murnau, exh. cat. (Cambridge, MA.: Busch-Reisinger Museum, Harvard University, 1980), 51, cat. 47 (color ill.).\\n\\nAnnegret Hoberg, Gabriele Münter, 1877–1962: Retrospektive, exh. cat. (München: Prestel, 1992), 40, 65, cat. 118 (color ill.).\\n\\nJames Wood, Treasures of 19th- and 20th-Century Painting, the Art Institute of Chicago (New York: Abbeville Press, 1993), 207 (color ill.).\\n\\nReinhold Heller, Gabriele Münter: The Years of Expressionism, 1903-1920, exh. cat. (Munich and New York: Prestel, 1997), 109, cat. 65 (color ill.).\\n\\nAnnegret Hoberg, Gabriele Münter (Munich and New York: Prestel, 2003), 28, 29, 76, pl. 42 (color ill.), as Stilleben mit Königin.\\n\\nVivian Endicott Barnett, The Chicago Lawyer Arthur Jerome Eddy and His Eclectic Art Collection (Philadelphia: American Philosophical Society Press, 2022), 109, 111, fig. 12.2 (color ill.).\\n\\nElizabeth Siegel, The Bradley Collection of Modern Art, exh. cat. (Milwaukee: Milwaukee Art Museum, 2025), 32 (color ill.).',\n",
       "   'exhibition_history': 'Munich, Der neue Kunstsalon Dietzel, G. Münter, Kollektiv-Ausstellung, March–April 1913 (traveled to Dresden, Frankfurt, and Stuttgart), cat. 21.\\n\\nArt Institute of Chicago, The Arthur Jerome Eddy Collection of Modern Paintings and Sculpture, Dec. 22, 1931–Jan. 17, 1932, cat. 13.\\n\\nArt Institute of Chicago, A Century of Progress Exhibition of Paintings and Sculpture, June 1–Nov. 1, 1933, cat. 761.\\n\\nSouth Bend, IN, Art Gallery, University of Notre Dame, The German Expressionists and Their Contemporaries: 50 Years of Fantasy and Frenzy, Dec. 7, 1969–Feb. 15, 1970, cat. 84a.\\n\\nChicago, Museum of Contemporary Art, German and Austrian Expressionism: Art in a Turbulent Era, Mar. 10–Apr. 30, 1978, no cat. no.\\n\\nSt. Petersburg, FL, Museum of Fine Arts, Expressionism and Its Legacy: German Art from 1905 to the Present: The Frankfurter Kunstkabinett Hannah Bekker vom Rath, Jan. 19–Feb. 24, 1980, cat. 9.\\n\\nCambridge, MA, Harvard University, Busch-Reisinger Museum, Gabriele Münter, between Munich and Murnau, Sept. 25–Nov. 8, 1980, cat. 47; Princeton, NJ, Princeton University Art Museum, Nov. 22, 1980–Jan. 18, 1981.\\n\\nMunich, Städtischen Galerie im Lenbachhaus, Gabriele Münter, 1877–1962: Retrospektive, July 29–Nov. 1, 1992, cat. 118; Frankfurt, Schirn Kunsthalle, Nov. 29–Feb. 10, 1993; Stockholm, Liljevalchs Konsthall, Apr. 4–May 31, 1993.\\n\\nMilwaukee, Milwaukee Art Museum, Gabriele Münter: The Years of Expressionism, 1903-1920, Dec. 5, 1997–Mar. 1, 1998, aat. 65; Columbus OH, Columbus Museum of Art, Apr. 18–June 21, 1998; Richmond, VA, Virginia Museum of Fine Arts, July 31–Sept. 21, 1998; San Antonio, TX, Marion Koogler McNay Art Museum, Nov. 3, 1998–Jan. 3, 1999.',\n",
